analysis:
Both changed files are test-only. EngineV2ProductionWiringTests.swift has a single changed line (312), where the test helper's switch now handles `.toolCall, .toolCallDelta` by skipping the event. The supplied units only show the unchanged tail of that file (lines 1221-2472). They contain no production code and no security-relevant logic change. The visible tests cover existing controls, with no behavior change in this PR:
- fail-closed forced tool_choice handling (rejection before submit, no visible text before a validated call);
- rejection of forged internal schema metadata on the local acquire path;
- media requests bypassing the bridge;
- the cacheSalt tenant scope threaded into the request (TB-007/T-041);
- cancellation propagation to the engine (T-010);
- KV-backend fallback reason clamped on the heartbeat.

SegmentedFleetGeometry.swift has a doc-comment-only change at lines 97-99. It rewords the comment on `maximumPrefillChunk` to say the value is the largest schedulable chunk, max(plain chunk, solo stripe). The code at lines 99-103 is unchanged, so the test fixture's computation is unchanged.

The new `.toolCallDelta` event case implies a production-side change, probably streaming tool-call deltas, that is outside the supplied units. Integration should check that the production streaming path for tool-call deltas preserves the forced tool_choice fail-closed validation (no visible text or unvalidated calls exposed before validation) and the encryption of response chunks (T-008). This PR's supplied test changes cannot confirm that. No findings arise from the supplied evidence.
